      "title": "Non-College Work-Study| Mellon Grant, Student Research Assistant",
      "description": "Non-College Work-Study|  Mellon Grant, Student Research Assistant - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Non-College Work-Study|  Mellon Grant, Student Research Assistant 497012 Part-Time Closing on: Oct 27 2026 Humanities & Social Sciences Add to favorites View favorites Department : Humanities & Social Sciences Salary : $12.00 per hour Description : JOB TITLE: Student Assistant DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Performs moderately complex technical, office, and clerical duties, some of which may require an automated system and accurate typing skills, as well as a degree of responsibility and judgment. Duties may include but are not limited to: • Data entry of forms into an automated system • Filing, sorting, copying and alphabetizing documents • Assists with mail • Answers phone calls, takes messages and greets visitors • Higher-level administrative tasks • Editorial assistance • Higher level technical skills; duties are specialized or technical requiring exceptional and diversified skills • Performs other related duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Moderately complex knowledge of computer hardware and software • Moderately complex knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, and database software. • Experience utilizing computer software applications. • Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Qualifications: • Current student of the University of Houston-Downtown • One year of experience in a college/university environment All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Recommended postings Non-College Work-Study| MDCOB Student Tutor 497031 Academic Affairs-Business Part-Time The Marilyn Davies College of Business is seeking qualified tutors to assist students in their studies and academic pursuits. Non Co