    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/campus-recreation-member-services-program-director-i-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Campus Recreation Member Services Program Director I",
      "description": "Campus Recreation Member Services Program Director I  - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Campus Recreation Member Services Program Director I 496873 Full-Time Campus Recreation Add to favorites View favorites Position Description Department : Campus Recreation Salary : $56,800 - $64,600 Description : University of Houston is a Division I university with over 47,000 undergraduate and post graduate students enrolled and is one of the most diverse student populations in the nation. UH has strong athletic programs and is in the Big 12 Athletic Conference. The Campus Recreation and Wellness Center Natatorium serves as home to the six-time champion varsity swimming and diving team. UH is committed to supporting all students, faculty and staff and is a Jed Campus. Benefits include employer paid health coverage, retirement through the Teacher Retirement System, Power Up Wellness program, professional development opportunities, and staff scholarships available for eligible employees. Directs an ongoing university program to ensure that prescribed activities are carried out in accordance with its mission and/or specified objectives. Prepares short- and long-term goals and objectives. 1. Plans, develops and administers methods, strategies and procedures for meeting program objectives; directs and oversees the daily activities of staff members. 2. Prepares and monitors the annual budget and ensures that expenditures are within budget allocation. 3. Directs and coordinates personally, or through subordinate personnel, activities concerned with carrying out the objectives of the program. 4. Directs the preparation of and reviews reports and records of activities to ensure progress is being accomplished toward specified program objectives; modifies or changes methodology as required to redirect activities and attains objectives. 5. Analyzes trends within program areas, maintaining expert awareness of program information and change needs. 6. Formulates, implements, and maintains appropriate policies and procedures concerning program administration. 7. Manages and administers grant for program, including meetings, communication coordination, scholarships and other operations. 8. May prepare or participate in the preparation of proposals to obtain grants from state and federal agencies, and private foundation sponsors. 9. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. MQ: Education: Requires a thorough understanding of both theoretical and practical aspects of an analytical, technical or professional discipline; or the basic knowledge of more than one professional discipline. Knowledge of the discipline is normally obtained through a formal, directly job-related 4 year degree from a college or university or an equivalent in-depth specialized training program that is directly related to the type of work being performed. Experience: Requires a minimum of three (3) years of directly job-related experience. Additional Job Posting Information: - Department is willing to accept education in lieu of experience. - Department is willing to accept experience in lieu of education. The Program Director for Member Services provides strategic leadership and comprehensive oversight of all Campus Recreation Member Services operations. This role ensures alignment, consistency, and effectiveness across member-facing functions while directly supervising the Program Manager for Member Services and maintaining accountability for fiscal management, compliance, systems administration, and long-term operational planning. This position reports to the Sr. Associate Director; evening and weekend hours are required. Job Duties: Responsibilities will include but are not limited to: • Provide direct supervision, mentorship, evaluation, and professional development oversight for the Program Manager and student staff, ensuring effective execution of day-to-day operations. Establish expectations, priorities, and performance standards for Member Services operations. • Provide oversight of all Member Services functions, including memberships, access control, program registrations, locker rentals, and point-of-sale operations. • Provide strategic leadership for member experience initiatives, ensuring services, processes, and interactions align with departmental goals for customer satisfaction, accessibility, and operational excellence. • Serve as the departmental administrator for the Campus Recreation management software platform; provide strategic direction for configurations, access, and functionality; and act as primary liaison with software vendors and university partners. • Provide leadership and accountability for the Member Services budget, including pro shop operations, payroll processes, financial reporting, and inventory systems. • Oversee fiscal forecasting, monitoring, reconciliation, and compliance to ensure alignment with university financial policies, MAPP, and SAM requirements. • Assess, evaluate, and mitigate risk within Member Services to ensure compliance with university, local, state, and industry standards; contribute to departmental risk and safety planning; and ensure policies and procedures are consistently applied. • Lead and support strategic initiatives focused on member recruitment, engagement, and retention. • Build and maintain relationships with internal and external partners, academic units, and affiliate groups; provide high-level support for invoicing, payment coordination, and business services processes. • Oversee the development and analysis of administrative duties, assessment, and semester reports related to Member Services operations. • Contribute to long-term operational and strategic planning efforts for Campus Recreation. • Evening and weekend hours are required as needed. • Perform other duties as assigned in support of Campus Recreation and divisional objectives. QUALIFICATIONS: A bachelor’s degree in business, recreation, sport management, hospitality management or related field. Master's degree preferred. Excellent written and verbal communications skills and attention to detail. Demonstrated proficiency in creating positive customer experience and the ability to lead and manage student staff. Experience utilizing Fusion software is preferred. Candidate must possess American Red Cross CPR, AED, First Aid certifications and instructor certifications; if not already certified, they must be obtained within the first six months of employment. APPLICATIONS: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled; however, priority review will begin September 25, 2026. Applicants must apply online at the University of Houston, Human Resources page at careers.uh.edu. Please submit cover letter, resume and list of 3 references with online application. Please ensure when completing the application that resume and cover letter are both loaded for the specific position being applied for. The University of Houston System and its universities are an Equal Opportunity Institution. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) dd97fce1 Last Name (required) 0382124e Email (required) 5f69d8ca Cell number d8815efc 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1