      "title": "Psychological Counselor- College of NSM",
      "description": "Psychological Counselor- College of NSM - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Psychological Counselor- College of NSM 496801 Full-Time Counseling & Psychologic Svcs Add to favorites View favorites Department : Counseling & Psychologic Svcs Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : Provides mental health services to the campus community, including one or more of the following services: individual, couples and group counseling and therapy; crisis intervention; consultation and outreach services. 1. Provides individual, couples and group counseling to students. 2. Participates in the development and delivery of support, awareness, outreach and consultation services to the campus community. 3. Provides initial assessment and on-call services to clients with personal concerns and maintains appropriate case documentation, supervision and evaluation records. 4. Performs clinical assessments and refers individuals to other resources as needed. 5. Develops and conducts outreach seminars, workshops, and programs. 6. May collaborate with other campus departments to create and implement programs for the campus community. 7. Assists in the supervision and training of interns, practicum students, and/or graduate students in counseling. 8. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. MQ: Requires application of advanced principles, techniques and theory in a professional discipline or a thorough general business management knowledge. Knowledge of this level is typically obtained through a directly job-related Master's degree or equivalent formal training in a recognized field of specialization that is directly related to the type of work being performed. Requires a minimum of one (1) year of directly job-related experience. Requires technical certification or licensing directly related to the job, as specified on a job description addendum. Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s degree in Counseling Psychology, Clinical Psychology, or Social Work. Licensure is required at the time of interview. We welcome applicants who do not have prior counseling center experience, provided candidates clearly articulate how their experience in other settings can be translated to a counseling center and higher education environment. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong clinical skills, sound professional judgment, and a commitment to continued professional development. Desired Qualifications Candidates who are three or more years post-licensure and have experience and expertise in one or more of the following areas: • A broad range of client presenting concerns • Short-term/brief therapy • Crisis intervention • Outreach and prevention programming General Responsibilities: This position is embedded within the College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics (NSM). The Embedded Counselor (EC) will have a split schedule, with approximately 80 percent of their time dedicated to serving NSM students and 20 percent at Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS), serving undergraduate and graduate students, staff, and faculty. The EC’s primary responsibility will be providing mental health counseling, consultation, and outreach to NSM students. The EC will establish and maintain a visible service presence within NSM, including networking and promoting CAPS services; assessing and addressing barriers to seeking mental health services; and collaborating with NSM administration, faculty, and staff to identify and address the clinical and programmatic needs of NSM students. The EC will provide individual, couples, and group services within a short-term therapy framework; facilitate mental health workshops and other outreach programming; adhere to stepped-care principles when assessing a student’s fit for services; provide crisis intervention and assessment; and engage in consultation and outreach activities. This position will include regular evening hours, with occasional weekend hours based on programmatic and service needs. About CAPS: The University of Houston’s Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS) is a vital department within the Health and Well-Being (HWB) portfolio. We work closely with our HWB partners, which include the Student Health Center; Campus Recreation; UH Wellness; Justin Dart, Jr. Student Accessibility Center; and Cougars in Recovery. Together, we are committed to fostering a culture of care that promotes the success of our students, faculty, and staff. We are proud to be a designated Jed Campus. CAPS is accredited by the International Accreditation of Counseling Services and offers an APA-accredited internship in Health Service Psychology. We have a multidisciplinary team consisting of licensed psychologists, doctoral- and master’s-level mental health professionals, and advanced graduate trainees in counseling, clinical, school psychology, and social work. Within our Stepped Care model, our services include triage, essential skills workshops, single-session therapy, group counseling, and short-term couples and individual counseling. We also offer a wide range of resources and outreach programs, including “Let’s Talk,” QPR, and on-demand trainings on a variety of mental health topics. The Embedded Counselor role provides an opportunity to work closely with an academic college while remaining connected to a multidisciplinary counseling center team, offering both specialized engagement with NSM students and broader clinical and professional opportunities within CAPS. About the College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics: The College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service in the physical and biological sciences, computer science, and mathematics. With six academic departments, including Biology and Biochemistry, Chemistry, Computer Science, Earth and Atmospheric Sciences, Mathematics, and Physics, it serves more than 6,000 undergraduate, master’s, and Ph.D. students. NSM students are preparing to be the next generation of scientists, health care professionals, computer scientists, and mathematicians who will address and solve local, national, and global challenges. About the University of Houston: The University of Houston is a Division I university with more than 48,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students enrolled. As a leading public research university, UH offers a dynamic academic environment with extensive opportunities for collaboration across disciplines. UH has strong athletic programs and is a member of the Big 12 Athletic Conference. The University of Houston is an Equal Opportunity institution. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Discover the Space City: Houston is one of the nation’s largest and most diverse metropolitan areas and offers an exceptional quality of life with a vibrant arts and culture scene, world-class museums, professional sports, extensive dining options, and numerous opportunities for outdoor recreation. The city is home to the Texas Medical Center, NASA’s Johnson Space Center, and a thriving economy with opportunities across numerous industries. Houston also offers easy access to the Gulf Coast and is a major international travel hub. Note: We will notify you in advance of making contact with any of your references. References may be contacted prior to an invitation for a campus visit. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 9ad16048 Last Name (required) 554d9a10 Email (required) eb6fb3e6 Cell number ce98c121 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Aust