      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Fellow - Mechanical Engineering - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Post Doctoral Fellow - Mechanical Engineering 497019 Full-Time Mechanical Engineering Add to favorites View favorites Department : Mechanical Engineering Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : Possesses, understands, and applies a comprehensive knowledge in area of specialization. Develops understanding and skills to allow for completion of assignments that cross fields of specialization. Develops leadership and management skills. 1. Receives/Reviews progress and evaluates results of experiments or projects under control or supervisory responsibility. 2. Recommends changes in research, testing or experimental procedures. 3. May be responsible for a single highly technical and complex piece of research equipment. 4. May review and evaluate the effectiveness of personnel. 5. May plan for and assign personnel to projects under control. 6. Operates with latitude for unreviewed action. 7. May receive general supervision conferring with higher levels only in unusual situations. 8. Performs other job-related duties as required. Position Summary We are seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate to work on an automated robotic system for surface damage detection and additive repair. The project combines 3D scanning, computational geometry, and collaborative robot control into an end-to-end pipeline — from scanning and damage detection through toolpath generation and robot-executed repair. The postdoc will work across both the algorithms and hands-on robotics sides of the project. Responsibilities - Develop algorithms for 3D surface damage detection, repair surface reconstruction, and conformal toolpath planning - Program and operate a collaborative robot arm for automated scanning and material deposition - Implement calibration routines, coordinate transforms, and robot motion strategies - Conduct physical experiments to validate system performance on test specimens - Develop software tools (Python, C++) for pipeline automation and operator interfaces - Publish in peer-reviewed journals and support proposal writing Required Qualifications - PhD in Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, or closely related field - Strong Python skills; working knowledge of C/C++ - Background in computational geometry, 3D mesh/point cloud processing, or sensor-robot calibration - Hands-on experimental research experience Preferred Qualifications - Experience with robot programming and control - Experience with additive manufacturing, cold spray, or thermal spray - Familiarity with 3D scanning systems or robot SDKs (ROS, vendor APIs) - Background in surface metrology or defect detection MQ: Requires singular knowledge of a specialized advanced professional discipline or the highest level of general business knowledge, normally acquired through attainment of a directly job-related terminal degree or equivalent formal training in a recognized field of specialization that is directly related to the type of work being performed. No experience is required. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) db1e1968 Last Name (required) c00e2606 Email (required) 11bea6e7 Cell number 751eba86 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) 