    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/visiting-assistant-professor-counseling-houston-texas-united-states-5517d03b-76c0-4908-bc1b-46a9e2afd74d": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling 497050 Full-Time Leadership & Policy Analysis Add to favorites View favorites Department: Transformative Leadership, Counseling, & Innovation Salary: Commensurate with Experience/Education Description: The Department of Transformative Leadership, Counseling, and Innovation at the University of Houston-Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for the position of Visiting Assistant Professor in its CACREP-accredited Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and growth of the counseling program, teach graduate counseling courses, and provide service to the program, university, and profession. This position will be for Spring 2027 and may be renewed based on program need. The Visiting Assistant Professor may apply for a tenure-track position if one is advertised and the required qualifications are met. Applications are accepted only through the UHCL Job Opportunities website. To apply, please complete the online application and attach a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statements of research and teaching interests, and evidence of teaching excellence. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled, with priority given to applications received by October 15, 2026. Interviews will take place online, and a teaching demonstration will be part of the final interview process. Duties: Teach graduate courses across the counseling curriculum, with particular emphasis on clinical mental health counseling Contribute to curriculum development and accreditation data collection and documentation Provide clinical supervision to practicum and internship students Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with community agencies and clinical partners Maintain an active counselor educator identity through professional engagement, practice, scholarship, service, and advocacy, as appropriate to the faculty role Participate in college activities and serve on program or college committees Participate in program, college, university, and professional service activities Qualifications Required: An earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program Evidence of a counselor and counselor educator identity through sustained professional engagement in at least two of the following areas: counseling-related professional development and renewal; professional service and advocacy; ongoing counseling practice; or research and scholarly activity commensurate with the faculty role Texas LPC licensure or eligibility for Texas LPC licensure Excellent communication skills Preferred: Successful university teaching experience Evidence of or potential for scholarly activity Demonstrated professional or academic service Experience providing clinical mental health counseling Experience teaching clinical mental health counseling students Experience using a learning management system and teaching in online or hybrid formats Experience with CACREP accreditation processes Experience providing clinical supervision to practicum or internship students Required Attachments by Candidate: Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Teaching Philosophy or Statement, Evidence of Effective Teaching Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Recommended postings Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling 497050 Academic Affairs-College of Edu Full-Time College of Education Web Content Specialist 496989 University Advancement-Marketing & Communications Full-Time Division of University Advancement Maintenance Tech I 496995 VP, Admin & Finance-FMC Full-Time Division of Administration and Finance Custodian 496994 VP, Admin & Finance-FMC Full-Time Division of Administration and Finance Electrician 496996 VP, Admin & Finance-FMC Full-Time Division of Administration & Finance Technical Systems Specialist 496953 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-Information Resources Full-Time Division of Administration and Finance 281–283–7600 2700 Bay Area Boulevard, Houston, TX 77058 © 2026 University of Houston–Clear Lake Maps and Directions Emergency Information University of Houston System University Police Fraud & Non-Compliance Hotline Campus Safety Directory Human Resources TRAIL (Statewide Search) State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Public Information Act Fraud Reporting Compact with Texans Linking Notice Privacy Notice University Policies Report It Faculty and Course Profiles Emergency Resource Card Texas Veterans Portal Campus Carry Anti-Discrimination (Title VII) Sexual Misconduct Reporting and Awareness (Title IX) Mental Health Resources Web Accessibility Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Profile link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
